# Batch launchers MUST arrive CRLF. An LF-only .cmd runs NOTHING under cmd.exe -
# no output, no error, exit 0 - so a clone made with core.autocrlf=false, or on a
# non-Windows machine, would produce a launcher that silently does nothing. Pinned
# here rather than left to whoever cloned it; test/sqlexpress-backup.test.ps1
# asserts the working tree matches.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# PowerShell and the C# source run on Windows. Keeping them CRLF in the working
# tree avoids a diff storm the first time someone edits one in a Windows editor.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cs  text eol=crlf

# Vendored, byte-for-byte. The console serves this out of the exe and a test
# compares the served bytes against this file, so it must not be rewritten.
